*** Keywords ***
Create Timestamps Results Message
    [Documentation]  This keyword prepares the test message with all collected timestamps.
    [Arguments]      ${timestamps}

    ${msg}=                                                 Evaluate  '\\n'.join([f"{distn}: {timestamps}" for distn, timestamps in $timestamps.items()])
    Set Test Message                                        Responsiveness Timestamps:\n${msg}


Responsiveness Teardown
    [Documentation]  This keyword deactivates the cell switch off power saving period if activated.

    ${back_to_initial}=                                     Get Variable Value  ${initial_delta}  ${False}
    IF  ${back_to_initial}
        delta_configurator.set_parameters_for_dist_names_via_delta_recommissioning
        ...                                                 objects_dict=${back_to_initial}
    END


Update Delta
    [Arguments]    ${delta}  ${dist_name}  ${param}  ${new_value}  ${old_value}
    Evaluate       $delta.setdefault($dist_name, {}).update({$param: $new_value})
    Evaluate       $initial_delta.setdefault($dist_name, {}).update({$param: $old_value})
    
    
Verify BTS And VM Time Match
    [Arguments]    ${bts_type}
    ${time_matched}=                                       Run Keyword And Return Status    
    ...                                                    Check If BTS And VM Time Match    
    ...                                                    bts_type=${bts_type}
    IF    not ${time_matched}
        Fail    For the proper interpretation of results, the VM and BTS times must match.
    END


Calculate Start And End Time Of Power Saving Period
    [Documentation]  This keyword calculates the start and end time of the power saving period based on the
    ...              current time and the provided duration and offset. Default offset is 5 minutes from now.
    [Arguments]      ${duration}
    ...              ${start_time_offset}=5

    ${now}=                                                 Get Current Date    result_format=datetime
    ${start_time}=                                          Add Time To Date    ${now.replace(second=0, microsecond=0)}  ${start_time_offset} minutes
    ...                                                     result_format=datetime
    ${end_time}=                                            Add Time To Date    ${start_time}  ${duration} minutes
    ...                                                     result_format=datetime
    [Return]                                                ${start_time}  ${end_time}
